  "detail": "Thank you: the adoption checks, the explicit lease, the digest and the start/stop cancellation all held up in review. One delivery gap was reproduced. If the daemon stops after a delivery push lands but before `publishedSha` is saved (for example during a deploy restart), and the base then advances, the resumed delivery merges the new base, pushes a different head with the old lease, is refused as stale, and the run ends needs_human. Main fails the same way today, but `publishedSha` now makes it cheap to fix. Required: at both `pushBranch` call sites, save the head about to be pushed as `ctx.state.publishingSha` (documented next to `publishedSha`) before the push. After a successful push, set `publishedSha` to it and clear `publishingSha` in the same save. When delivery or `deliverVerifiedDraft` resumes with `publishingSha` set, read `remoteBranchSha` before merging or pushing. If the remote holds exactly `publishingSha`, record it as `publishedSha` and clear `publishingSha`; otherwise just clear it. Never adopt any other remote value. Test: stop at the post-push save, advance the base, restart; delivery merges the new base and pushes it under a lease on the earlier pushed head, and the PR opens. A control where the remote holds something else still refuses."
